# 🏗️ Complete Build Plan: Telephony + Campaign + Agent Management → 100%

## Scope: 3 Areas to Complete

### Area 1: Telephony Engine (14% → 100%)
### Area 2: Campaign Engine (17% → 100%)  
### Area 3: Agent Management (10% → 100%)

---

## Phase 1: Database Schema (ALL models first)

Add the following **30 new Prisma models** to `schema.prisma`:

### Telephony Models (12 new)
1. `Extension` — SIP extensions for agents
2. `SipTrunk` — SIP provider connections
3. `OutboundRoute` — Call routing rules
4. `IvrMenu` — IVR tree definitions
5. `AcdQueue` — Automatic Call Distribution queues
6. `QueueMember` — Agent-to-queue assignments
7. `Skill` — Agent skills (language, product knowledge)
8. `AgentSkill` — Agent-skill-level mapping
9. `SkillRule` — Skill-based routing rules
10. `RingGroup` — Ring groups with members
11. `RingGroupMember` — Extension-to-ring-group mapping
12. `TimeCondition` — Business hours routing rules

### Campaign Models (8 new)
13. `CampaignContactList` — Imported contact lists for campaigns
14. `CampaignContact` — Individual contacts in a campaign list
15. `Transmission` — Per-contact communication pipeline (ICTCore pattern)
16. `CallSpool` — Active/completed call attempts per transmission
17. `SpoolResult` — Result log for each call attempt
18. `DncEntry` — Do-Not-Call compliance list
19. `DialerConfig` — Per-campaign dialer settings (predictive/preview/progressive)
20. `AgentScript` — Dynamic call scripts with branching

### Agent Management Models (10 new)
21. `AgentSession` — Login/logout session tracking
22. `PauseCode` — Break type definitions (Lunch, Meeting, Training)
23. `AgentPause` — Individual agent pause records
24. `AgentCapacity` — Max concurrent conversations per agent
25. `AssignmentPolicy` — Auto-assignment rules (round-robin, fair-dist)
26. `WallboardConfig` — Saved wallboard layouts
27. `QualityForm` — Call quality evaluation forms
28. `QualityEvaluation` — Individual call evaluations
29. `CsatResponse` — Customer satisfaction survey responses
30. `CannedResponse` — Quick reply templates

### Enums (8 new)
- `ExtensionType`, `QueueStrategy`, `DialerMode`, `TransmissionStatus`
- `SpoolStatus`, `AssignmentMethod`, `PauseType`, `SessionStatus`

---

## Phase 2: Backend — NestJS Modules

### Telephony Module (`src/telephony/`)
- Full CRUD controllers + services for: Extensions, SIP Trunks, IVR Menus, ACD Queues, Ring Groups, Time Conditions, Skills
- FreeSWITCH ESL integration service (connect, originate, hangup, transfer, conference)
- WebRTC signaling gateway (WebSocket for SIP.js ↔ FreeSWITCH)
- CDR (Call Detail Records) service with real reporting queries
- Call recording management (list, play, download, search)

### Campaign Module (`src/campaigns/` — enhance existing)
- Dialer engine service (predictive pacing, preview, progressive, power modes)
- Transmission pipeline service (create → spool → attempt → result)
- DNC compliance service (check before every call, import/export DNC lists)
- Campaign progress tracker (real-time stats via WebSocket)
- Contact list import service (CSV/Excel → CampaignContact records)
- Agent script service with branching logic

### Agent Module (`src/agent-management/` — new)
- Agent session service (login/logout tracking, shift hours)
- Agent pause/break service (track break time by type)
- Agent capacity service (max concurrent load management)
- Auto-assignment service (round-robin, least-busy, skill-based)
- Wallboard data service (real-time queue stats, agent stats)
- Quality evaluation service (form builder + evaluation CRUD)
- CSAT service (post-call survey, ratings)
- Canned response service (quick reply templates)
- Agent monitoring gateway (WebSocket for live supervisor view)

---

## Phase 3: Frontend — Next.js Pages

### Telephony Pages
- `/telephony` — Dashboard overview
- `/telephony/extensions` — Extension CRUD + SIP config
- `/telephony/trunks` — SIP trunk management
- `/telephony/ivr` — Visual IVR builder (React Flow)
- `/telephony/queues` — ACD queue management
- `/telephony/ring-groups` — Ring group config
- `/telephony/recordings` — Call recording player + search
- `/telephony/cdr` — Call detail records with filters + export
- `Softphone` component — WebRTC dialer (SIP.js) in AppShell

### Campaign Pages (enhance existing)
- `/campaigns/[id]/dialer` — Dialer control panel (start/pause/stats)
- `/campaigns/[id]/contacts` — Contact list with import
- `/campaigns/[id]/progress` — Real-time progress dashboard
- `/campaigns/dnc` — DNC list management
- `/campaigns/scripts` — Script builder with branching UI

### Agent Management Pages
- `/agent-console` — Unified agent workspace (calls + chat + lead info)
- `/supervisor/monitoring` — Live agent monitoring dashboard
- `/supervisor/wallboard` — Big-screen wallboard view
- `/supervisor/quality` — Quality evaluation forms + grading
- `/supervisor/csat` — CSAT reports + review
- `/settings/assignment` — Assignment policy config
- `/settings/pause-codes` — Break type management
- `/settings/canned-responses` — Quick reply management

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated
- `npx prisma validate` — Schema validates
- `npx prisma db push` — All tables created
- `npm run start:dev` — Backend starts with 0 errors
- `npm run build` — Frontend builds with 0 errors

### Manual (Browser)
- Create extension → assign to agent → make test call
- Create campaign → import contacts → start dialer → see progress
- Agent logs in → sees console → takes calls → goes on break
- Supervisor sees live dashboard with agent statuses
- Wallboard shows real-time queue metrics

---

## Execution Order
1. Schema first (all 30 models + enums)
2. Backend services (all 3 areas in parallel)
3. Frontend pages (all 3 areas)
4. Wire everything together + verify
